    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Christian Yelich** (72.16) and **Junior Caminero** (68.21). **Christian Yelich** is our premier play, benefiting from a favorable 4.50 xERA matchup against Singer and a significant boost from his dynamic platoon advantage. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** remains a must-start at 3B; despite a slight park penalty, his high base projection and favorable order placement in the #3 hole provide the stability we need. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-focused leadoff hitters, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (65.79) and **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77). While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** faces a difficult challenge against Skenes, his +14% platoon edge and the wind-aided park factors keep his efficiency well within our strong start range.\n\nManagement spent significant time evaluating the final utility spots, ultimately favoring **Caleb Durbin** (62.19) over **Chase Meidroth** (42.46). While **Chase Meidroth** projected adequately, his negative park and platoon factors against Leahy dragged him below the threshold required to displace **Caleb Durbin**, whose efficiency against Dobnak is buoyed by a substantial 14% SP skill advantage. We remain cautious regarding **Carson Benge** (48.42); he is the most volatile start of the day, as a -10% penalty for opposing pitcher Cole creates a precarious floor that requires close monitoring throughout the game.\n\nThe primary risk today involves the Skenes matchup for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Pedro Ramirez**. While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** has the statistical profile to persevere, the combination of an elite arm and a catcher with a 1.89s pop time poses a legitimate threat to our stolen base production, our most vital category. **Pedro Ramirez** was ultimately benched, falling just under our 40.0 efficiency floor, as we prioritize **Jacob Gonzalez** (47.07) for his wind-advantaged profile. We will be tracking the status of our remaining depth, including **Yordan Alvarez**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Casey Schmitt**, and **Luis Pena**, to ensure we remain optimized for the final push.",
